# This driver applies to a merge git performs, and to nothing else. GitHub does not read this file:
# neither the mergeability it reports on a pull request nor the merge its button performs consults
# a merge driver, so a branch that both sides have touched in a file named here reads as conflicting
# on GitHub while `git merge` on a clone resolves it silently and correctly. That is why it is not
# what keeps parallel branches apart in `changelog/`, where a change records itself in a file of its
# own and there is nothing for either merge to resolve.

# DEFECTS.md is appended to by any branch that finds one, and each entry is a whole section under
# its own heading, so two branches adding entries have nothing in common to conflict over. Union
# merge keeps both. Deletion is the other half of the file's rule — an entry leaves in the change
# that fixes it — and union merge does not resolve a delete against an edit, so a branch that fixes
# a defect while another edits the same entry conflicts there, which is the right outcome: somebody
# has to read both sides.
#
# On GitHub none of that applies, and the report is the misleading one described above. It is a
# smaller version of the same defect the changelog had — DEFECTS.md::defects-entries-share-one-file
# holds it, with the gate its fix owes.
DEFECTS.md merge=union
